msgid ""
"Use ``LoadContext::read_config`` and ``read_file`` during load. They "
"fingerprint the bytes actually read and declare dependencies. Keep loaded "
"state unchanged throughout the build. If we read other files ourselves, "
"we declare their paths with ``declare_dependency`` and add a fingerprint "
"of the loaded values with ``add_cache_key``. Selected environment values "
"go there too. The context only appends, so the fingerprints the helpers "
"recorded cannot be erased. A plugin must not depend on undeclared "
"changing data."
msgstr ""
"Durante la carga, use ``read_plugin_config`` y ``read_plugin_file``. "
"Registran huellas de los bytes realmente leídos y declaran dependencias. "
"Mantenga el estado cargado sin cambios durante la compilación. Si lee "
"otros archivos por su cuenta, declare sus rutas en "
"``session.dependencies`` y añada una huella de los valores cargados a "
"``session.cache_key``. Añada también los valores del entorno utilizados. "
"No borre las huellas del SDK ni dependa de datos cambiantes sin declarar."

#: ../../plugins.rst:263
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The host includes identity, configuration, dependencies, cache key, "
#| "builder, language and generated assets in cache invalidation. Each "
#| "build gets private sessions. Reading workers serialize callback "
#| "access; callbacks need not be thread safe. Native callbacks cannot be "
#| "interrupted by a process deadline. Installed programs have a deadline "
#| "per whole request, including pipe writes."
msgid ""
"The host includes identity, configuration, dependencies, cache key, "
"builder, language and generated assets in cache invalidation. Hooks take "
"``&mut self``. When reading workers share a session, the host serializes "
"calls through a ``Mutex``, so plugins need no synchronization. Installed "
"programs have a deadline per whole request, including pipe writes."
msgstr ""
"El anfitrión incluye identidad, configuración, dependencias, clave de "
"caché, constructor, idioma y recursos generados al invalidar la caché. "
"Cada compilación tiene sesiones privadas. Los hilos de lectura serializan "
"el acceso a callbacks; estos no necesitan ser seguros entre hilos. Un "
"plazo de proceso no puede interrumpir callbacks nativos. Los programas "
"instalados tienen un plazo por solicitud completa, incluidas las "
"escrituras en pipes."

